            "description": [
                "<b>Neural Network Library for C++ / C# / Python</b>",
                "Dynamic Link Library",
                "Was built on C++, then C#, and then Python",
                "Consisted of my own implementation of neural networks.",
                "Was made to learn how neural networks work and was also assisted by AI while learning. However, the AI tools had constantly brought me towards incorrect path of learning on how to build an image recognition software.",
                "Was made to somehow build an AI system for CCTVs with object detection, which never happened due to the highly theoretical nature of my learning path.",
                "Relied on various academic papers and books such as <i>C++ Neural Networks and Fuzzy Logic</i>, <i>Fuzzy Logic and Neural Networks</i>, <i>Modern Algorithms for Image Processing</i>, and many more but none of them helped me build an AI system practically since all of them are too theoretical or too focused on mathematical or scientific computations. All of these books were suggested by ChatGPT.",
                "It was abandoned due to several school projects and a thesis project, but I plan to work on it again under a different project and under a different learning path."
